From c5a1e04242673893b511084b425a32e0816f9adc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zigoljube <ziga.drev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 23:08:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(dkg-memory): community-gateway fallback for
 full-fidelity remote viewing

Viewers without a local node now resolve the memory panel through the
community gateway (RFC deployment profile 2) over the tailnet, seeing the
same layers/decisions/evidence/subgraphs as the operator, labeled
'Resolved via community gateway' (blue) vs 'Verified through your node'
(green). Resolution order: localStorage override -> local explorer probe
-> gateway. Discovery mode remains the last resort. E2e covers all three.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Zigoljube <ziga.drev@gmail.com>
